data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 90% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 29 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"398.6944827586207\" cy=\"55.65517241379308\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 90% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 225 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.82\" cy=\"53.591111111111104\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(81%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":4.89035,"lon":114.94006,"n":503,"n_cities":213,"name":"Bandar Seri Begawan","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.5340000000000001,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.3947058823529413,"n":51,"obs":0.6078431372549019,"sig":true},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.5340000000000001,"mean":0.6724444444444444,"n":45,"obs":0.6666666666666666,"sig":false},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.7877358490566038,"n":53,"obs":0.6981132075471698,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.8656097560975611,"n":41,"obs":0.8292682926829268,"sig":false},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9242372881355932,"n":59,"obs":0.7457627118644068,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9624137931034483,"n":29,"obs":0.896551724137931